ion, up 92% year over year, and networking alone grew 199%.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161, e205, e210; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e202 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to total revenue of $91 billion for Q2 FY2027.\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e255; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e204 [fact; David Moadel, citing NVIDIA’s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, including Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161, e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e205 [fact; David Moadel, citing NVIDIA’s reported results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier, reflecting surging demand for the Spectrum-X Ethernet and NVLink interconnect systems that travel with every rack-scale Blackwell deployment.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e201; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e209 [fact; 247Wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e210 [fact; TIKR author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center segment revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year; the quarter is not specified.\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e201, e249; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e227 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta Platforms, Anthropic, and OpenAI starting late 2026 and continuing into 2027.\n    Quote: However, Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\n- e239 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e122; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e242 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported quarterly revenue of about $35 billion, up 198% year over year and a record.\n    Quote: In the recent quarter, for example, the company reported revenue growth of 198% to about $35 billion dollars, a record level.\n- e243 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba57